                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The 25 environments times 30 second left-right mobile-tier controls of avoiding bullets means you can beat the game in 12 min and 30 seconds.\n\nEvery time you lose, you have to add 30 seconds to it because you have to play the previous level if you take three hits during those 30 seconds. Losing becomes unlikely as soon as you realize the safe spots of the particular level and where the level hazards are and what they look like.\n\nSome color choices are questionable. It would be better if the danger tiles and projectiles was color-coded with a designated color such as purple or highlighted.\n\nThe psychedelic mode seems to be about having a trippy moving pattern in the background.\n\nIt is okay as a simple casual game. At least it is not as annoying as Super Hexagon that people compare this one against.\n\nAs a fair disclosure, I would not care about this game in the slightest unless I got it for like 10 cents from a keyshop to a record a playthrough of it. Considering it has a below-average MRRP (Manuifacturer's Recommended Retail Price),",
